    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nBuilding the latest git version, gives me this warning.\ngcc-16.2.1\n\n```cmake\n[100%] Linking C executable ../../bin/nvim\n/opt/src/neovim/src/nvim/input_cmdatom.c: In function ‘atom_visual_span.part.0’:\n/opt/src/neovim/src/nvim/input_cmdatom.c:1028:3: warning: ‘memcpy’ writing between 18446744073709551614 and 18446744073709551615 bytes into a region of size 0 [-Wstringop-overflow=]\n 1028 |   kv_concat_len(keys, tail.data, tail.size);\n      |   ^\n/opt/src/neovim/src/nvim/input_cmdatom.c:1027:3: note: at offset 2 into destination object of size 2 allocated by ‘xrealloc’\n 1027 |   kv_concat(keys, \"gv\");\n      |   ^\n[100%] Built target nvim_bin\n```\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nmake distclean && make CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/sw/neovim && make install\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n-\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nlatest\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nlinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub",
